[LUNI.13.11] **Currency is not part of this edition.** This section and
`unit fx_pair` ([LUNI.4.6]) are deferred: no conforming compiler or runtime is
obliged to implement them. The compiler **must** refuse every construct that
reaches them, with `DS_VALIDATE_FINANCE_DEFERRED`, at the construct:

- an import of `units.currency` ([LUNI.16.5]);
- a `unit fx_pair` declaration;
- a `.to_currency(...)` call;
- a `.round(...)` or `.round_to(...)` method call ([LUNI.13.5]).

The function `round(x)` ([LEXP.3.2]) is not a currency construct and is
unaffected. The section's own diagnostic codes stay allocated.
